WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.769
-♪ Best Friends Challenge ♪

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.538
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.106
-Now, this game works
like "The Newlywed Game,"

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:08.507
but for friends.

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:11.444
We're gonna take turns reading
questions about each other

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.845
from the Best Friends Box,

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:16.549
and then we're gonna try
to write down the same answer.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:17.984
We didn't plan any of this out.

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.452
In fact, I've played this
with Tina Fey,

00:00:20.452 --> 00:00:22.955
Justin Timberlake, Viola Davis,

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:26.158
and I've never gotten one
question right with any of them.

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:28.494
But anyways -- But let's
change that all tonight.

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:29.862
So, here we go.

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:31.798
This is your marker
and your pad here.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:35.568
I'll read
the first question here.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:37.771
All right.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.038
Okay.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:42.374
Demi,
if I were a Disney Princess,

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:43.776
which one would I be?

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.978
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.978 --> 00:00:52.251 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:56.189 line:0%
[ Clock ticking ]

00:00:56.189 --> 00:01:00.460 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.361
All right. Time's up.
-[ Laughing ] Okay.

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:04.997
[ Laughter ]
-There's no time. All right.

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:06.199
Demi, you can show it
to that camera.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:08.601
What did you write?
What Princess would I be?

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:09.869
[ Drumroll ]
Oh, I didn't know that.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.371
Cinderella is your --
-Yeah.

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.005
-Yes.

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:15.341
-I said Belle from
"Beauty &amp; the Beast."

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.443
[ Laughter ]
[ Sad trombone notes ]

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:18.844
But I put --
-"Mama"?

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:21.481
-I put "Maybe Moana"
just in case.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.382
I didn't know.
I was just hedging my bets.

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:24.651
My girls love Moana now,

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.085
so I didn't want to take
their princess.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.253
-Oh, got it.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.287
-But I would be Belle,
'cause that's more my --

00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:30.356
-Cute.
-Remember, I'm 43 years old.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.658
All right.
Good.

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:33.692
Here we go.
So, yeah.

00:01:33.692 --> 00:01:35.427
-Okay.
-All right. Here we go.

00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:37.229
-Ready?
-Yes.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:38.397
Is that question one?
-Yes.

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:40.065
-Yeah, perfect.
All right. Here we go.

00:01:40.065 --> 00:01:43.135
-If Demi was stranded
on a deserted island...

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:44.270
-Oh, no.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.305
-...what one thing
would she bring with her?

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:48.674 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:50.143
-Definitely not spicy pickles.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.845
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.414
Oh.
What would she bring?

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:56.415
Oh!

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:58.417
[ Clock ticking ]

00:01:58.417 --> 00:02:00.686 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.021
[ Marker scribbling ]

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.789
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:05.391
[ Marker clacks ]

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.593
Okay.
Ready?

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:07.694
-Okay.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.395
-Here's my answer.

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.298
Your two dogs --
Batman and the other one.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.399
-[ Laughing ]
"The other one."

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.967
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.101
And Cinderella.

00:02:16.101 --> 00:02:18.137
-Oh, that's right.
Cinderella and Batman!

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:19.439
What did you say?

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:20.873
-I said my iPhone.

00:02:20.873 --> 00:02:22.375
-Oh, my gosh!
Come on!

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.909
[ Sad trombone notes ]
-I'm a terrible owner.

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:25.011
I'm a terrible --

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.078
-You were talking
about your dogs.

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:27.146
You love your dogs.

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:28.514
-I know,
but if you had your iPhone,

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.182
you might get service,
and you might could call

00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:31.684
your way off the island.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.319
-I don't even get service
in New York City.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.621
I mean, come on.
Deserted island.

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:36.922
All right,
I will read the next question.

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:39.225
Here we go.
Ready?

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.626
-I should have said my dogs.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:43.395
-If we were going to binge-watch
a TV show together,

00:02:43.395 --> 00:02:45.031
what show would we pick?

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.599
I know.
Here we go.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.901
[ Clock ticking ]

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.637 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:51.637 --> 00:02:53.006
[ Marker clacks ]

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:54.741
-This is not gonna be right.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:58.110
-This is going to be right.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.012
My BFF, what did you say?

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:02.949
It's like --
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.718
What did I say?
"Walking Dead."

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.386
-I know.
-That's similar.

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:08.688
-It's my favorite show.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.356
-I said "Riverdale," which is --

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.558
[ Laughter ]
[ Sad trombone notes ]

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:13.859
That's too scary for me.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:15.161
-Really?
-I can't do that.

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.796
"Riverdale", Archie --
this is scary enough for me.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.564
There's a murder.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:20.233
Jughead's involved.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.735
It's a great show, "Riverdale,"
on The CW.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.203
All right.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:26.906
-Okay, ready?
-Yeah.

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:30.710
-If we became one person
and had to combine our names,

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.446
what would our new name be?

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:35.448
[ Clock ticking ]

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:40.619 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:43.088
[ Marker clacks ]

00:03:43.088 --> 00:03:45.758
[ Laughs ]

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:46.993
-Do we do it at similar times?

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:49.095
We got to get this one, BFF.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.563
[ Drumroll ]
All right.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:54.033
We have to combine our names.
What is your answer?

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.268
-Jemetria.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:57.303
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.812
-Similar.

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:06.979
Jemmi!

00:04:06.979 --> 00:04:08.180
There you go.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.749
Demi Lovato, everybody!

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:12.585
Demi's performing for us
later in the show!

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.587
Check out her new album,
"Tell Me You Love Me,"

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:16.055
on September 29th.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.558
And her Fabletics workout gear
is available now.

